{"agent":"wave-orchestrator","data":{"how":"In _round_and_current_tree, only read commit_source_tree(repo, ev['reviewed_head']) when recorded_content and tree_sha are both empty (a --commit round) and no worktree is readable; a round that DID name a tree, even an opaque dirty one, fails closed ('the round names no tree it reviewed').","rule":"","seen_in":[],"summary":"reviewed_head is generic round evidence (the head the diff was captured from), present on worktree and --commit rounds alike; a fallback that treats it as the reviewed tree must fire only when the round named no tree of its own, else a dirty-tree round is read as the clean commit and triage can pass work no reviewer saw.","supersedes":[],"tags":[],"title":"reviewed_head is recorded on every round, not only --commit reviews","why":"Fixing B-critic-refutation-pass-needs-tree-after-merge I first resolved the reviewed tree from ev.reviewed_head whenever no worktree stood. qwen/deepseek caught it: a dirty-tree round also records reviewed_head (the worktree HEAD), so the fallback misread a dirty fingerprint (<head>+opaque> as the clean commit. The fallback must be gated on the round naming NO tree_sha/source_tree at all."},"id":"e022c31d29506a883c37e3f72","kind":"lesson.recorded","lamport":122441,"schema":1,"subject":"L4c24696616","ts":"2026-11-01T16:15:26.911686Z"}
